      "hypothesis": "Applying the adapted Tukey's rule and the new distance metric to other partitional algorithms like fuzzy c-means and k-medoids will similarly improve their clustering accuracy.",
      "rationale": "Since the techniques successfully addressed outlier influence and distance metric limitations in k-means, they should theoretically benefit other centroid-based or partitioning techniques.",
      "evidence": "Section 7 states: 'In future work, the adapted Tukey’s rule and the new distance metric will be applied to various clustering algorithms such as fuzzy c-means and k-medoids.'",
      "sections": [
